title: October 2025

@ko_consolidation_2025
# prose-audit: Grade A — Tusk's demand, the three memberships asked to disappear and Lewica's one available move are stated on a single page, and the count separates the legal form KO adopts from whether its leader survives adopting it. Each stance names what it costs rather than moving a hidden meter.
title: KO asks its three parties to dissolve themselves
subtitle: PO, Nowoczesna and Inicjatywa Polska vote on becoming one party; Lewica may take one public stance and will be quoted taking it
face-image: img/poland/events/donald-tusk-2023.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 24
order: 10
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2025 and month = 10 and ko_collapsed = 0 and ko_2020_alliance_broken = 0
on-arrival: {!
const koConventionRoll =
    Math.floor((this.random.uint32() / 4294967296) * 9) - 4;
// One meter carries this convention and every later KO crisis: what the
// coalition year has already cost KO, what the polls say about it, and
// whether it kept the Palace it spent 2025 fighting for. A party that missed
// the 2020 runoff arrives at every one of its own conventions with the same
// unanswered question, and the components price it.
Q.ko_cohesion = Math.max(5, Math.min(95, Math.round(
    64 -
    Math.max(0, (Number(Q.ko_coalition_dissent) || 0) - 20) * 0.8 +
    ((Number(Q.ko_poll) || 27) - 27) * 0.9 +
    (Q.pres_2025_winner_key == "right" ? -8 : 6) -
    (Q.ko_hegemony_broken
        ? 6 + Math.max(0, Number(Q.ko_2020_humiliation) || 0) * 0.12
        : 0) +
    koConventionRoll
)));
Q.ko_convention_done = 1;
Q.ko_consolidation_stance = "No public stance";
Q.ko_consolidation_outgoing_leaders =
    "Donald Tusk (PO), Adam Szłapka (Nowoczesna) and Barbara Nowacka (Inicjatywa Polska)";
Q.news_headline =
    "KO's three parties open a convention on dissolving themselves";
!}

= October 2025 — Three parties, one hall

<span class="party-ko"><b>Donald Tusk</b></span> wants the organisations printed under KO's name to stop
existing. Platforma Obywatelska, Nowoczesna and Inicjatywa Polska would
dissolve into one registered party with one treasury, one list and one set of
candidate rules.[? if not p2050_greens_absorbed: Zieloni never entered the
negotiation and keep their own registration whatever the hall decides.?][? if
p2050_greens_absorbed: Zieloni are not a fourth component: they dissolved into
Poland 2050 in 2024 and have no registration for this convention to preserve.?]

The three memberships are not voting on a slogan. <span class="party-ko"><b>Adam Szłapka</b></span> would
exchange Nowoczesna's registration for a current inside somebody else's party.
<span class="party-ko"><b>Barbara Nowacka</b></span> would exchange Inicjatywa Polska's veto for a quota.
PO's regional structures would exchange the right to be consulted for the
right to be organised. Each of them can count what KO's year has cost before
handing over the keys.

[? if ko_hegemony_broken: All three boards can also count back further than
that. The reason a Civic component was ever expected to give up its
registration was that KO would deliver the presidency and the government; in
June 2020 it delivered **[+ ko_2020_r1_share +]%** and no second ballot, and
every delegate in the hall has heard the number quoted at them since.?]

[? if ko_cohesion >= 70: The arithmetic is finished before the speeches begin.
The component boards have their numbers, and the only live argument is what
the losing minorities are promised in writing.?]
[? if ko_cohesion >= 52 and ko_cohesion < 70: The votes exist for something,
but not obviously for dissolution. The delegates who arrived undecided are the
ones being worked on in the corridors.?]
[? if ko_cohesion >= 38 and ko_cohesion < 52: Two component boards have
already told their members that nothing will be signed today, and the platform
party is trying to establish which of them meant it.?]
[? if ko_cohesion < 38: This is less a convention than a hearing into the last
year, and the people being asked to dissolve their parties are the ones asking
the questions.?]

Lewica holds no ballot here. It can say one thing in public before the
components vote, and whatever it says will be read out in the hall by whoever
it helps.

- @ko_consolidation_back
- @ko_consolidation_abstain
- @ko_consolidation_open_door

@ko_consolidation_back
title: Say publicly that one KO is good for the coalition
subtitle: Makes the single party materially more likely and buys goodwill; costs us the argument that we are a different politics from it.
on-arrival: ko_cohesion += 10; ko_relation += 6; progressive_credibility -= 3; party_unity -= 2; ko_consolidation_stance = "Public backing"; news_headline = "Lewica publicly backs KO's single party"

Our statement is read from the platform within the hour: the coalition's
second party wants one reliable counterparty rather than three signatures for
every agreement. Wavering delegates are handed a reason that comes from
outside their own quarrel. Our own organisers ask, in public and by name, why
we spent the morning helping a liberal party solve its structural problem
while ours remains unsolved.

- @ko_consolidation_result: Wait for the component ballots

@ko_consolidation_abstain
title: Treat the dissolution as KO's own business
subtitle: No influence in either direction; nobody quotes us in the hall and nobody owes us anything afterwards.
on-arrival: public_trust += 2; ko_consolidation_stance = "No public stance"; news_headline = "Lewica declines to take a side in KO's convention"

We say that a party's legal form is decided by its members and that we are not
members. The line survives contact with journalists, which is more than most
lines manage. It also means that whichever wing wins the hall will remember
that we were not there when it needed a sentence.

- @ko_consolidation_result: Wait for the component ballots

@ko_consolidation_open_door
title: Tell whoever loses that Lewica has room for them
subtitle: Hardens the components against dissolution and brings us organisers; KO will call it a raid for the rest of the term.
on-arrival: ko_cohesion -= 12; ko_relation -= 7; local_network += 3; ko_collapse_shock += 8; ko_consolidation_stance = "Open door to the losers"; news_headline = "Lewica opens its door to KO's losing minorities"

We say, before the vote rather than after it, that any councillor or organiser
about to lose their party has somewhere to go. Delegates who were ready to
concede discover they have an alternative, and boards that were ready to sign
discover they have a reason not to. KO's leadership does not treat this as a
comment on internal democracy; it treats it as recruitment, and says so.

- @ko_consolidation_result: Wait for the component ballots

@ko_consolidation_result
title: The component ballots are counted
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
const group = function(id) {
    return (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
        return record.id == id;
    });
};
const po = group("po");
const nowoczesna = group("nowoczesna");
const ipl = group("ipl");
const greens = group("greens");
const koParty = group("ko_party");
const cohesion = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Number(Q.ko_cohesion) || 0));
Q.ko_cohesion = cohesion;
// Succession rule, used here and again whenever KO breaks: a president holds
// no party office, a politician who has joined Lewica cannot lead KO, a
// collapsing party goes to whoever holds the apparatus, and a surviving one
// goes to its larger wing.
const available = function(name) {
    return name != Q.president_name &&
        !(name == "Rafał Trzaskowski" && Q.trzaskowski_joined_left);
};
const progressiveWing =
    (Number(Q.ko_social_liberal_share) || 0) >=
    (Number(Q.ko_classical_liberal_share) || 0);
const successor = cohesion < 45
    ? (available("Marcin Kierwiński")
        ? "Marcin Kierwiński"
        : "Barbara Nowacka")
    : (progressiveWing
        ? (available("Rafał Trzaskowski")
            ? "Rafał Trzaskowski"
            : "Barbara Nowacka")
        : (available("Radosław Sikorski")
            ? "Radosław Sikorski"
            : "Marcin Kierwiński"));
const incumbentHolds = cohesion >= 58 && (Number(Q.ko_poll) || 0) >= 23;
Q.ko_leader_previous = Q.ko_leader;
Q.ko_convention_failed = 0;
Q.ko_consolidated = 0;
Q.ko_individual_defectors = 0;
const componentStatus = function(status) {
    for (const component of [po, nowoczesna, ipl]) {
        if (component) {
            component.active = 1;
            component.kind = "party";
            component.parent = "Koalicja Obywatelska";
            component.legal_status = status;
        }
    }
};
if (cohesion >= 72) {
    Q.ko_consolidated = 1;
    Q.ko_merger_result = "One registered KO party";
    for (const component of [po, nowoczesna, ipl]) {
        if (component) {
            component.active = 1;
            component.kind = "current";
            component.parent = "Koalicja Obywatelska";
            component.legal_status = "internal KO current";
            component.exclusive_seats = 0;
        }
    }
    if (koParty) {
        koParty.active = 1;
        koParty.legal_status = "registered party";
        koParty.organisation = 84;
        koParty.cohesion = cohesion;
        koParty.mp_count = Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0;
        koParty.sejm_mps = Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0;
    }
    Q.ko_collapse_shock = Math.max(
        0,
        (Number(Q.ko_collapse_shock) || 0) - 12
    );
    Q.ko_coalition_dissent = Math.max(
        0,
        (Number(Q.ko_coalition_dissent) || 0) - 6
    );
} else if (cohesion >= 55) {
    Q.ko_merger_result = "A federation of three parties";
    componentStatus("federated component party");
    if (koParty) {
        koParty.active = 0;
        koParty.legal_status = "federal electoral alliance";
    }
} else if (cohesion >= 40) {
    Q.ko_merger_result = "Convention adjourned without a decision";
    Q.ko_convention_failed = 1;
    componentStatus("surviving allied party");
    if (koParty) {
        koParty.active = 0;
        koParty.legal_status = "electoral alliance";
    }
    Q.ko_collapse_shock = (Number(Q.ko_collapse_shock) || 0) + 22;
    Q.ko_coalition_dissent = (Number(Q.ko_coalition_dissent) || 0) + 6;
} else {
    Q.ko_merger_result = "The convention broke up";
    Q.ko_convention_failed = 1;
    componentStatus("separate party after a failed convention");
    if (koParty) {
        koParty.active = 0;
        koParty.legal_status = "electoral alliance in name only";
    }
    Q.ko_collapse_shock = (Number(Q.ko_collapse_shock) || 0) + 45;
    Q.ko_coalition_dissent = (Number(Q.ko_coalition_dissent) || 0) + 12;
    Q.ko_cohesion = Math.max(5, cohesion - 10);
}
Q.ko_leader = incumbentHolds ? Q.ko_leader : successor;
Q.ko_leader_changed = Q.ko_leader != Q.ko_leader_previous ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.ko_leader_changed) {
    Q.ko_coalition_dissent = (Number(Q.ko_coalition_dissent) || 0) + 4;
}
// The open door only produces crossings where the convention actually left
// people without a party to belong to.
if (Q.ko_consolidation_stance == "Open door to the losers" && cohesion < 62) {
    const availableKoSeats = Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0));
    const defectors = Math.min(
        Math.max(2, Math.round((62 - cohesion) / 7)),
        availableKoSeats
    );
    Q.ko_individual_defectors = defectors;
    Q.ko_seats = availableKoSeats - defectors;
    Q.left_seats = Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_seats) || 0) + defectors;
    Q.left_progressives_seats =
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_progressives_seats) || 0) + defectors;
    Q.left_new_generation_seats =
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_new_generation_seats) || 0) + defectors;
    Q.nowa_lewica_seats =
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.nowa_lewica_seats) || 0) + defectors;
    if (
        Q.government_party == "ko" &&
        Q.government_has_confidence && !Q.caretaker_government
    ) {
        Q.government_support_seats = Math.max(
            0,
            (Number(Q.government_support_seats) || 0) - defectors
        );
    }
    for (const component of [nowoczesna, ipl, po]) {
        if (component) {
            component.mp_count = Math.max(
                0,
                (Number(component.mp_count) || 0) -
                    Math.round(defectors / 3)
            );
            component.sejm_mps = Math.max(
                0,
                (Number(component.sejm_mps) || 0) - Math.round(defectors / 3)
            );
        }
    }
}
if (greens && !Q.p2050_greens_absorbed) {
    greens.active = 1;
    greens.allied = 1;
    greens.legal_status = "allied separate party";
}
Q.ko_merger_stage = 7;
Q.news_headline = "KO convention: " + Q.ko_merger_result;
!}

= [+ ko_merger_result +]

[? if ko_merger_result = "One registered KO party": PO, Nowoczesna and
Inicjatywa Polska cease to exist as parties and continue as named currents
inside one registered organisation. KO now stands on a single party list at
the 5% threshold instead of a coalition list at 8%, and it can discipline its
own candidates for the first time. The losing minorities keep guaranteed
representation inside it, which is the price the majority paid to get the
vote.?]
[? if ko_merger_result = "A federation of three parties": The components
refuse dissolution and sign a federation instead. Lists, money and arbitration
run under a written formula between parties that still exist, so any one of
them can still veto the others. Our partner remains broad, negotiable and
permanently one board meeting away from a crisis.?]
[? if ko_merger_result = "Convention adjourned without a decision": Nothing is
signed. The platform adjourns to a date that is not fixed, and every component
returns home with its registration, its debts and its grievance intact. KO
will fight the next election in the legal form it was trying to escape.?]
[? if ko_merger_result = "The convention broke up": Two component boards walk
out before the ballots are counted and say so on camera. What remains is an
electoral alliance in name, a shared logo and three organisations that have
now publicly told their members the other two cannot be trusted with the
lists.?]

[? if ko_leader_changed: **[+ ko_leader +]** leaves the hall as KO's leader in
place of **[+ ko_leader_previous +]**, who could not hold a party this
divided and this far down in the polls. The change is real: the offices, the
list decisions and the person we negotiate with are no longer the same.?]
[? if not ko_leader_changed: **[+ ko_leader +]** holds the leadership. The
convention decided KO's legal form without deciding who runs it, which is the
outcome an incumbent with the numbers always prefers.?]

[? if ko_individual_defectors > 0: Our open door was used. **[+
ko_individual_defectors +]** MPs cross to Lewica with their organisers, and KO
records every one of them as a raid rather than a resignation.?]

[? if ko_convention_failed: A party that cannot decide what it is does not
stop having to decide. The question returns, and next time it will not arrive
as a convention.?]

- @ko_merger_finish
- @ko_merger_invite_greens

@ko_merger_finish
title: Return the result to the coalition table
go-to: poland_event_queue

@ko_merger_invite_greens
title: Invite the still-separate Greens into a future broad Left party
subtitle: Requires a strong Left and a social mood that rewards consolidation.
view-if: p2050_greens_absorbed = 0
choose-if: left_poll >= 14 and party_system_left_pull >= 18 and ko_relation >= 30
unavailable-subtitle: The Greens prefer their existing shelter while Lewica lacks leverage.
on-arrival: left_realign_invite_greens = 1; progressive_credibility += 3; ko_relation -= 4; local_network += 2; news_headline = "Lewica offers Zieloni a protected current in a broader Left party"

We use the convention's result to offer Zieloni a protected place in a future
broad Left. Green organisers gain an alternative shelter; KO treats the offer
as recruitment from an ally that deliberately remained separate.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the invitation to Zieloni
